! agent_p92.strap -- MCP, printed page 92: THE DISK ANALYSER.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.99, header "PAGE NUMBER 92"
! (confirmed by rendering the header band: "PAGE NUMBER   92",
! card id 18000495, PUNID 11C11IPL).
!
! THE PAGE IS BOX-HEADED "DISK ANALYSER", not a MOVE continuation.
! Lines 1-6 are the box and blanks; lines 7-40 all compile, thirty-
! four rows, 005210.40 through 005244.00.  Whether DISK ANALYSER is
! a sub-section of MOVE or a successor routine is not something this
! page settles, and nothing here asserts it.  The next box, on
! printed p.93, is "TRACK ANALYSER".
!
! THE PAGE IS CONTIGUOUS WITH printed p.93 AT ITS TAIL.  Line 40 is
! a one-half-word "B,T M1FA" at 005244.00, so the counter reaches
! 005244.40, and PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line 4 is "T MDK2" at
! 005244.40.  That was read, not computed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE ROUTINE DOES, in the page's own comments
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Get the unit table address (line 7), the relative address of the
! disk counter (8) and the counter itself (10); if the request is
! for a TRACK go to T MTRK on p.93 (11).  Otherwise set current and
! original arc from the counter (12-14), fetch the disk number
! (15), compare it against T M6BL -- the six blanks of printed p.83
! line 13 -- and branch to T MNULD if the disk is null (16-17).
! Not null: call the conversion subroutine at T MCONV with a return
! index of T MDK1 (18-19), add the converted number to the counter
! (21-26), subtract one (27), and reject through T MDSK3 if the
! result exceeds T MMAX = 4095 (28-29).  Store the maximum arc (30),
! pick up the reference number of the null IOD (31), and if there is
! none fall out to T M1FA (32).  If there is one, index into the
! SIOL table through T LIMB (33-35), reload the last counter (36)
! and update that file area's current and original arc too (37-40).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PRINTER'S ZERO IS AN OPEN C ON THIS PAGE <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! listing_typography.md 13d.  Nearly every 0 on p.92 prints with a
! break in its right side: line 7's location reads "CC5210.40" and
! line 18's second octal group reads "005223.C3".  Read at 900 dpi
! and compared with the SAME row's undamaged zeros, they are zeros.
! The one place this mattered is line 21's trailing hex byte, which
! reads "7C" at every resolution tried: it is 70.  The proof is in
! the column, not in the glyph -- line 36 is the SAME instruction
! with the count operand dropped, "LF,T SBDFT(T MXGA)", and prints
! "014000.06 70" with an undamaged 0, and the assembler compiles
! both forms with the same trailing byte 70.  A real C there would
! have made the count operand change bits 28-31, which it does not.
!
! A genuine B DOES appear, on line 27: "014000.32 B0".  Its glyph
! has the flat left stem and two bowls; set beside line 26's
! opcode "8B" and line 28's "80" at 1800 dpi the three are distinct.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> TWO LISTING MARKS <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 21 and 34 carry the asterisk after the LOCATION value that
! docs/listing_typography.md 12 records as open and unexplained.
! Both rows are in the checked set below and both match the printed
! BINARY OUTPUT character for character, so the mark changes no bit
! here either.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> SIX FORWARD SYMBOLS, ALL READ OFF A PRINTED NAME COLUMN <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page branches to six labels it does not define.  None of them
! is back-derived from this page's own BINARY OUTPUT column; each
! was read from the NAME and LOCATION columns of the page that
! declares it, which were rendered for this purpose:
!
!   T MDK2   005244.40   PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line  4
!   T MNULD  005250.40   PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line 10
!   T MTRK   005255.00   PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line 16
!   T M1FA   005262.00   PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line 23
!   T MDSK3  005263.40   PDF p.100 (printed p.93) line 29
!   T MCONV  005450.40   PDF p.105 (printed p.98) line  5
!
! listing_oracle.py's own docstring names this the house move --
! "any symbol defined outside the transcribed range given by SYN
! from its printed address" -- and warns that rows naming such a
! symbol verify only the opcode and modifier bits.  Here they verify
! more than that, because the addresses came from a DIFFERENT page's
! location column rather than from this page's binary column, so the
! agreement of e.g. line 11's "005255.34 02" is a real check that
! bit 18 and the BB modifier land where the assembler puts them.
!
! THAT HALF-WORD SELECT IS WHY THE .40s MATTER.  listing_oracle.py:
! "bit 18, the half-word select of a branch target, is the top bit
! of the octal pair".  T MNULD at 005250.40 is the second half-word
! of its word, so BAE prints 005250.76 (.40 + the .36 modifier) and
! BRZ prints 005250.74 (.40 + .34).  printed p.93 line 17 settles
! the modifier independently: "BRZ,T MDK" prints 005214.74 and
! T MDK is this page's line 12 at 005214.40, so BRZ's modifier is
! .34 and nothing on this page had to be assumed to get it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 27 IS "M-1", AND strap_asm NOW HAS IT <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "M-1(BU,12),$L+.52" at 005231.00, printed 000010.64 80
! 014000.32 B0.  When this page was first transcribed strap_asm
! raised KeyError 'M-1' and the row was deliberately LEFT OUT of the
! checked set rather than written as M+1, because compiling a
! knowingly wrong word into the one column this deck exists to check
! would have been worse than leaving the hole.  That was right.
!
! The hole is now closed from the PAGE, not from the assembler.
! opcodes.py's VFL_INT_WRITTEN_MINUS requires a PRIMARY SOURCE that
! spells the written-minus form on a VFL operation, and this line is
! one: it carries a VFL data description, (BU,12).  M-1 is M+1 with
! the invert-sign modifier -- the rule strip_fp_sign already carried
! as "M-" -> ("M+", 0, 1) -- and the bits agree independently: M+1
! prints ".22 B0" on printed pp.55, 71 and 73, M-1 prints ".32 B0"
! here, and 0o32 - 0o22 = 0o10 is exactly the bit that separates
! M- (.50 A0) from M+ (.40 A0).
!
! The row is assembled and CHECKED below, and line 28's re-anchoring
! SLC is gone with it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNAL SYMBOLS AND THEIR SOURCE PAGES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Index registers and the six-blank constant come from printed p.83,
! the file-area and unit-table offsets from p.84, the arc offsets
! from p.85.  T MMAX and T M6BL are given WITH THEIR DATA
! DESCRIPTIONS, because KF inherits the dds of its operand symbol:
! KF,T M6BL prints 060600.23 10 only when T M6BL is (BU,48,6), and
! KF,T MMAX,64 prints 014040.23 10 only when T MMAX is (BU,12).
! Both dds are printed on p.83 (lines 8 and 13).

        SLC, (8)5210.40

! ---- index registers, printed p.83 --------------------------------
TMX1    SYN, $1                      ! p.83 line 21
TMXD    SYN, $5                      ! p.83 line 25 -FILE AREA TBL IX
TMXG    SYN, $8                      ! p.83 line 28 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TMXI    SYN, $10                     ! p.83 line 30 -CONTROL WORD IX
TMXGA   SYN, $11                     ! p.83 line 31 -TEMPORARY INDEX
! ---- words and constants, printed p.83 ----------------------------
TMMAX   SYN(BU,12), (8)4630.0        ! p.83 line 8  -THE VERY MAX DISK REF
TM6BL   SYN(BU,48,6), (8)4631.10     ! p.83 line 13 -SIX BLANKS
TLIMB   SYN, (8)2155.0               ! p.83 line 15 = S BAPP
TDKSAV  SYN, (8)4652.0               ! p.83 line 42 -ADDR OF UNIT TABLE
! ---- table offsets, printed p.84 ----------------------------------
TDSKRF  SYN(BU,12), 25.48            ! p.84 line 10 -REF NUMBER
TDTRK   SYN(BU,1), 25.60             ! p.84 line 11 -ONE IF TRACK
TDKCT   SYN(BU,3), 25.61             ! p.84 line 12 -RELATIVE ADDRESS
TSBDFT  SYN(BU,12), (8)4737.05       ! p.84 line 18 -DISK ALLOC TABLE
TITRK   SYN(BU,1), 2.59              ! p.84 line 29 -TRACK CODE BIT
TINO    SYN(BU,48), 5.0              ! p.84 line 33 -THE NUMBER FOR DISK
! ---- file area table offsets, printed p.85 ------------------------
TORARC  SYN(BU,12), 5.06             ! p.85 line 12 -ORIGINAL ARC
TMXARC  SYN(BU,12), 5.38             ! p.85 line 13 -MAXIMUM ARC
TCUARC  SYN(BU,12), 6.06             ! p.85 line 14 -CURRENT ARC
! ---- forward labels, printed pp.93 and 98 -------------------------
TMDK2   SYN, (8)5244.40              ! p.93 line  4
TMNULD  SYN, (8)5250.40              ! p.93 line 10
TMTRK   SYN, (8)5255.0               ! p.93 line 16
TM1FA   SYN, (8)5262.0               ! p.93 line 23
TMDSK3  SYN, (8)5263.40              ! p.93 line 29
TMCONV  SYN, (8)5450.40              ! p.98 line  5

        SLC, (8)5210.40

! ---- DISK ANALYSER ------------------------------------------------
        LV, TMXG, TDKSAV             ! line 7  -GET UNIT TABLE ADDRESS
        L, TDKCT(TMXG), 45           ! line 8  -GET RELATIVE ADDRESS
                                     !           OF DISK COUNTER
        LV, TMXGA, $R                ! line 9
        L, TSBDFT(TMXGA), 64         ! line 10 -GET COUNTER
        BB, TITRK(TMXI), TMTRK       ! line 11 -IF TRACK
TMDK    ST, TCUARC(TMXD), 64         ! line 12 -SET CURRENT ARC
        ST, TORARC(TMXD), 64         ! line 13 -SET ORIGINAL ARC
        ST, TSBDFT(TMXGA), 64        ! line 14 -SAVE AS TRACK ROUNDS OFF
        L, TINO(TMXI)                ! line 15 -GET THE DISK NUMBER
        KF, TM6BL                    ! line 16 -LOOK FOR DISK NULL--
                                     !           BLANK
        BAE, TMNULD                  ! line 17 -IF NULL
        LVI, TMX1, TMDK1             ! line 18
        B, TMCONV                    ! line 19 -GO TO THE CONVERSION
                                     !           ROUTINE
TMDK1   BRZ, TMNULD                  ! line 20 -IF NULL -- ZERO
        LF, TSBDFT(TMXGA), 64        ! line 21 -RELOAD ACC
        BB, TITRK(TMXI), TMDK3       ! line 22 -IF TRACK
        +(BU,12), $R+.52, 64         ! line 23 -ADD THE CONVERTED NUMBER
        B, TMDK4                     ! line 24
TMDK3   +(BU,12), $R+.52, 67         ! line 25 -ADD THE CONVERTED
                                     !           NUMBER -- TRACK
TMDK4   ST, TSBDFT(TMXGA), 64        ! line 26 -UP DATE THE COUNTER

        M-1(BU,12), $L+.52           ! line 27 -SUBTRACT ONE FOR THE
                                     !           PROPER COUNT
        KF, TMMAX, 64                ! line 28 -LOOK FOR ILLEGAL DISK
                                     !           REQUEST
        BAH, TMDSK3                  ! line 29 -YES
        ST, TMXARC(TMXD), 64         ! line 30 -STORE THE MAXIMUM ARC
        L, TDSKRF(TMXG), 46          ! line 31 -GET THE REF NO. OF
                                     !           NULL IOD
        BRZ, TM1FA                   ! line 32 -IF NONE
        +(BU,18), TLIMB, 46          ! line 33 -ADD THE BASE ADDRESS
                                     !           OF THE SIOL TBL
        LV, TMXD, $R                 ! line 34
        LV, TMXD, 0.32(TMXD)         ! line 35 -GET FILE AREA OF
                                     !           NULL IOD
        LF, TSBDFT(TMXGA)            ! line 36 -GET LAST COUNTER
        BB, TDTRK(TMXG), TMDK2       ! line 37 -IF TRACK
TMDK1A  ST, TCUARC(TMXD)             ! line 38 -UPDATE CURRENT ARC
        ST, TORARC(TMXD)             ! line 39 -UPDATE ORIGINAL ARC
        B, TM1FA                     ! line 40

! NO "END" CARD.  The page prints none, and END's operand is the
! program's ENTRY POINT -- printed p.80 line 4's T PICA is that
! page's entry, and decks pp.85, 87, 88 and 89 carry no END at all.
! This page's first statement, line 7, is UNLABELLED, so there is no
! entry label to name and nothing to put on an END card.

